tion":0.0037423452029938763,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.00713,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Versigent PLC designs, manufactures, and distributes low- and high-voltage power electrical architectures. The company offers signal and data connectivity solutions, power distribution systems, high-voltage electrical distribution systems, and EV charging solutions. It serves automotive, commercial vehicle, energy and grid, and other industries. The company was founded in 2026 and is based in Schaffhausen, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph T. Liotine | CEO & Director | Age 52","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 138K people. Revenue per employee of $64K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $3K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $239 per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["Versigent PLC is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.9B market cap on $8.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 28% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 21-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $481M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $10.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 28% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 74% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 41% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headline